    "termsOfAccess": "Access to the restricted files may be requested for scholarly purposes, including replication, verification, and non-commercial academic research. Requests will be reviewed by the depositor and, where necessary, in accordance with Maastricht University data protection and research data management requirements.\n\nThe data, or part of the data, has been set to restrictive because the data is pseudonymous and therefore subject to the EU GDPR privacy regulations. According to our policy, the researcher who deposited the data will be informed about the access request. The depositor of the data might contact the requester for further consultation about the (re)use of the data. If the researcher decides to make the data available an agreement needs to be signed.\n\nUsers granted access must not attempt to identify participants, teams, or institutions; must not redistribute the data to third parties; must use the data only for the approved purpose; and must cite the dataset DOI in any resulting publication or output. Access may be refused or withdrawn if the requested use is incompatible with participant confidentiality, ethical approval, or applicable data protection requirements.",
